Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 27 CLINICAL DATA  The patient presents with a left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  4 0 CM   MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  BOTH COMPONENTS EXTENDING TO INKED MARGINS  NTOE  About 90 percent of the tumor is infiltrating  Foci of ductal carcinoma in situ are present at greater than one low power field from the main tumor mass  Multiple foci of lymphatic invasion are identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm yellow to tan red piece of tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hard area  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a gritty  yellow tan cut surface in the hard area  Tissue from this area is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  additional tissue from this area  including the closest margin  is submitted in A D  Representative sections from uninvolved breast are submitted in E H  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY   report_end  , No.
