cm from the superior margin  1 5cm from the inferior margin  and 2cm from the posterior margin  1cm from the lateral margin and 5cm from the medial margin  The gelatinous area around the nodule abuts the lateral supero posterior margin  A metal clip was found  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section containing the nodule and the surrounding gelatinous area to the different margins  with  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the nodule and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  containing the sections where a metal clip was identified   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral margin  radially sectioned showing a relationship of gelatinous area to margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial margin en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section away from gelatinous area  unremarkable parenchyma  Received fresh  and labeled  right breast additional lateral margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm fibrofatty soft tissue specimen  unoriented  The specimen is entirely inked black  serially sectioned to reveal fibrofatty top surface  The entire specimen is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  and labeled  right breast biopsy  needle localization   short stitch   anterior  long stitch   lateral  bowtie   cephalad   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm fibrofatty ovoid soft tissue specimen with a needle localization wire in place with stitches designating the different margins  short stitch   anterior margin  long stitch   lateral margin  bowtie stitch   superior margin  The long axis of the specimen is anteroposterior  The specimen is inked as follows  Superior   blue  inferior   black  medial   green  lateral   yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a firmer area containing two metal clips  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  located 0 6cm from the posterior margin  1 2cm from the medial margin  1 7cm from the superior margin  1 6cm from the inferior margin  and 1cm from the lateral margin  and 1 5cm from the anterior resection margin  No discrete masses are identified  The remainder of the specimen consists of yellow adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section that contained the metal clips to the closest margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Previous and following sections to the one containing the clip  showing possible scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of posterior margin  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section away from previous biopsy site  Received fresh and labeled  left axillary contents   is an 11 x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm fibrofatty specimen containing multiple lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 3cm in largest dimension  The large node is firm and ill defined  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  in toto   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One firm lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Multiple lymph nodes  in toto   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lymph node  bisected  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Rare tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomple