rs that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 28     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen consists of two parts  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast posterior lesion  is a piece fibroadipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm with a localizing wire and accompanying X ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm white firm area 0 2cm from nearest inked margin  Firm area is submitted in cassettes A through C  the rest in D and E  No frozen section is done  Also received fresh in frozen section lab  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast anterior lesion  is a 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying X ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm white firm area extending to an inked margin  Representative sections is frozen as frozen section  1  This material is saved frozen  The firm area is submitted in cassettes F through K  the rest in cassettes L th