atest length  and 0 3cm in width  The interface of the tumor with the surrounding breast parenchyma is grossly non infiltrative  No areas of hermorrhage or necrosis are seen  A representative section of the specimen is frozen as FX 1  and submitted as A  a section of the closest deep resection margin is submitted in B C  Representative sections from different areas of the tumor mass are submitted in D U  Sections taken from the cyst like area are submitted in H I  Representative sections of tumor interfacing with surrounding breast parenchyma in S T  A section containing a small comedo like area submitted in U  The surrounding breast parenchyma is sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty tissue  No additional masses are found  Representative sections of unremarkable breast parenchyma are submitted in V W  Section of the axillary tail reveals multiple  red  firm lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 2cm  All lymph nodes are submitted in W through BB  Received in a separate container   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name only is an REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm skin ellipse with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm adipose tissue  The surface of the skin ellipse and cut surface of the adipose tissue are unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in CC  Received in a separate container  labeled  lymph nodes  are three fragments of adipose tissue which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in total aggregate  The adipose tissue is dissected to reveal multiple  tan  firm lymph nodes  ranging in size from 0 3cm to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  All submitted in DD through EE  Received in a separate container   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number is an REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm  unremarkable skin ellipse with attached underlying adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm in greatest dimension  A representative section of skin is submitted in FF  Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGN