ast tissue  the larger measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm and the other  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the long axis into 10 sections numbered REMOVED_DATE with  1 containing the aspect through which the needle localization wire passed  On cut section  the specimen is primarily fibrous with a 0 5cm diameter  hemorrhagic cavity consistent with biopsy cavity present at one edge margin  sections 3 6   A 0 2cm metal cylinder is found within this cavity in section  6  Two additional fragments of breast tissue are inked blue externally  serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section  1  radial to end margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections  2 9  entire specimen  one per cassette   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section  10  radially to end margin  specimen entirely submitted    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Larger separate fragment  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller separate fragment  entirely submitted  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1  Immunohistochemical stains for keratin  p63  calponin and myosin were performed on a representative section of the tumor and confirm the presence of in situ and invasive ductal carcinoma  Addendum  1 by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  report_end  , No.
