Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 18 57 CLINICAL DATA  Status post excision REMOVED_DATE  with confirmation of breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM CLOSEST DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   2 INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOLID TYPE  SCANT  3 METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO 16 OF 27 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not identified  Ten of sixteen lymph nodes with metastatic carcinoma demonstrated extranodal extension  4 HEALING BIOPSY SITE WITH METAPLASTIC BONE FORMATION  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 26 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 1 705 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm breast specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm axillary tail  The breast specimen contains an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 9 9cm nipple containing skin ellipse  The nipple is grossly unremarkable  The skin ellipse contains a 4 6cm well healed scar in the inferior portion of skin ellipse  The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm white  firm  stellate mass deep to the previously noted scar  The stellate mass is 1 4cm from the closest deep resection margin  Other areas within the breast are firm  white  irregular  and contain multiple microcysts ranging from 0 1cm and less in greatest dimension  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow and separated by white fibrous strands and grossly unremarkable  The axillary tail is removed from the main specimen and dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging from 1 6cm to 0 3cm in greatest dimension  White  firm  hard areas are noted in many of the lymph nodes  SECTION CODE  A  closest resection margin  represented by deep resection margin B E  representative sections of the firm stellate mass F H  irregular  white  firm areas not associated with main mass I R  representative sections of lymph nodes  from axillary tail S  representative section of scar on skin ellipse and nipple  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE U